==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Rock Revengers''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''The One-Hit Wonders''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the other [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]], Sarukani has significantly different stats between Normal (spammable) and Evolved Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Sarukani can be used as a generalist midrange attacker, especially against [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] he outranges, but his use is recommended mostly against [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]].

One issue when facing zombies is killing them reliably, something that only armies with plenty of Zombie Killers can do. Sarukani is thus best paired with the likes of [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter]] and [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying]] to clear tough Zombie stages, as the main midrange attacker alongside Polevaulter, ensuring both a constant supply of Zombie-killing attacks and solid enough damage for other traits that may be present.

He is versatile enough to counter all common zombies except [[Cadaver Bear]] and [[Zamelle]].

==='''Evolved Form'''===
The Rock Revengers are generally less suited at fighting Zombies than the first form as they aren't constantly attacking un-burrowing/reviving Zombies, which can easily lead to a lot of damage building up, as well as undesired freeze or weaken. They, however, perform well against Cadaver Bear, Zamelle and Daboo thanks to the high health and range. Against other traits, their health, slow immunity and range makes them excellent as a backliner in usually uncomfortable positions for other long ranged attackers, such as when fighting [[Sunfish Jones]] and [[Croakley]]. In addition, their stats make them a viable, though expensive, backline attacker for everyday situations, not unlike [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] or [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]].

Bringing them for their combo is also worth considering in certain stages or in absence of 2-slots alternatives, as they are likely to be of use regardless.

==='''True Form'''===
Faster attacks, better health and weaken immunity make the One-Hit Wonders more reliable against groups of common Zombies, but they will still need support from other Zombie Killers to not get overwhelmed, a role that they themselves could be filling by reverting to the first form. Their forte is still as support in presence of ranged "big guys", with [[Winged Pigge]] now being added to the list of foes they counter.

=== Talents ===

One-Hit Wonder's Savage Blow is massive, don't underestimate it because it's a 20% chance. If this hits, it will do massive damage to any unit, if not completely destroying any Angel and Zombie enemy in the game. Talents also bring it toxic immunity, mainly for [[Zollow]] and [[Heavenly Herald Papuu|Papuu]], but this also works against other enemies like [[Gobble]] too. Lastly, Freeze immunity helps for [[Zir Zeal]] and [[Chickful A]], but this lets it be used against any [[Henry]] stages as well. Overall, these are good talents for an already good unit.

